      "writtenOn": "2013-08-29T03:25:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you are calling this method from other files, you are probably in need of another interface method (get_consumer_with_secret or \"get_consumer_secret(consumer_id)\").  A _prefix should indicate that it is private (though python doesn\u0027t enforce this).  An alternative would be to make get_consumer take an option \"include_secret\" option.  \n\nI think a new interface method is more correct in this situation.",
